WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:05.240
Contrary to your common movie villain, the
walking dead are simple, primal, and animalistic.

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:09.400
Still, there are all kinds of complex mysteries
surrounding their abilities and tendencies

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:12.580
that tend to get glossed over or go completely
unexplored.

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:18.060
When we think of zombies, we tend to think
of shambling undead corpses that ravenously

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:22.800
hunt for human flesh all day and all night…
a habit that will continue unabated so long

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:25.310
as they're still hooked up to those all-important
brains.

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:26.320
Are you with us so far?

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:34.060
Sure, it's disturbing… but it's also just
kind-of confusing.

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:39.020
Sometimes, we'll see zombies that are deformed
beyond recognition but are still quite snappy

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:39.640
and energetic.

00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:44.520
And sometimes, highly decomposed zombies can
still move with the same vim and vigor they

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:47.740
once demonstrated in gentler, less zombified
times.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:52.200
In fact, some zombies seem to move even faster
than when they were alive.

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:58.820
"As zombies began to outnumber humans, well
that's when you had to cut all emotional ties."

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:03.620
These idiosyncrasies can be somewhat explained
when a film is constrained to a very specific

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:04.160
timeline.

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:09.160
I Am Legend is set three years after the initial
outbreak, and it doesn't stray too far from

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:12.880
there, allowing for some continuity in regards
to those dastardly Darkseekers.

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:17.220
But in shows like The Walking Dead, the issue
of deterioration has become a challenge.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:21.180
Much like the act of watching The Walking
Dead has become a challenge.

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:23.480
To give you an example, let's compare and
contrast.

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:27.540
Here are some terrifyingly low-key zombies
from Season One of The Walking Dead:

00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:39.980
And here are some zombies from Season Eight
of The Walking Dead:

00:01:48.940 --> 00:01:53.560
Yeah, they look a little worse for the wear,
but they move like they've hardly aged a day…

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:55.440
so what exactly is their secret?

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:56.220
Olay?

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:58.979
"Vitamin enriched, fights seven signs of aging.

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:02.080
In four weeks, skin looks up to 10 years younger."

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:07.400
As the years pass us by and the seasons drag
on and on and on, it raises an obvious question:

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:12.120
How and why are these jerks still moving around
at virtually the same speed as when they first

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:13.080
turned into zombies?

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:13.900
Anyone?

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:27.280
Every movie seems to have its own origin for
the zombie plague — if they bother to explain

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:27.860
it at all.

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:33.280
But none of them try to answer the most basic
question: What exactly goes on in these zombies'

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:33.780
heads?

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:38.660
When it comes to brain function, there's absolutely
no consistency in the world of these cold,

00:02:38.660 --> 00:02:40.160
clammy, bloodthirsty creeps.

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:45.320
Some zombies move with superhuman speed and
are capable of effortlessly lifting people

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:46.520
into the air with their bare hands.

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:51.600
Meanwhile, other zombies are seemingly incapable
of even taking a brisk afternoon stroll.

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:55.100
For every goal-oriented zombie with drive
and determination…

00:02:57.780 --> 00:02:58.820
"Brains!”

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:04.280
... there's a whole mess of zero-ambition
zombies who can barely keep it together.

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:05.260
No dreams.

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:06.120
No ambition.

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:15.799
This raises more puzzling questions: What
level of brain function do these undead shambling

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:16.860
nightmares operate on?

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:19.060
Are some zombies smarter than others?

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:23.840
"... More brains."

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:28.200
And if these zombies are technically dead,
how do they have any brain function in the

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:28.940
first place?

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:30.020
Any insights?

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:38.240
Sorry, here's something else that really bugs
us: Some zombies have the wherewithal to be

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:40.860
fast as hell, bounding about like young gazelles.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:45.160
Other times, they're just shuffling along,
slow as snails and twice as slimy.

00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:46.860
Like these boring zombies.

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:51.340
If there really are a few rudimentary thoughts
still floating around inside these zombie

00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:54.260
brains, where exactly is the line drawn?

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:57.880
Do all the same rules apply to mean-spirited
zombie monkeys?

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:00.400
What about majestic zombie horses?

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:08.640
And some zombies are apparently MENSA material.

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:13.239
Remember that scene in World War Z, when the
undead hordes built a towering zombie ladder

00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:14.240
to scale the wall?

00:04:22.420 --> 00:04:25.680
Yeah, that's not the kind of thing you can
just build on pure instinct.

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:29.040
Even for a zombie movie, that type of behavior
is kind of a stretch.

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:33.380
Here's something else about zombies that we're
just supposed to accept … because we're

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:36.540
never given any kind of rational explanation
at all.

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:39.080
Why do zombies always want to eat human beings?

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:40.520
It's so excessive.

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:45.000
We're not talking about some desperate compromise
made in order to survive on a lifeboat.

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:48.640
Not that zombies don't like to go on a sailing
expedition every once in awhile.

00:04:57.890 --> 00:05:02.160
When it comes to zombies and their love of
human flesh, we're talking about a culinary

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:03.440
preference like no other.

00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:08.140
Whenever someone turns into a zombie, it usually
takes only a matter of seconds before they

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:10.220
start munching on the nearest person they
can find.

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:13.600
Why do zombies like human flesh and not, say,
fast food?

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:18.300
“I want my Whopper."

00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:23.530
In a moment of weakness, why can't your standard-grade
zombie just engulf a bag of Cool Ranch Doritos

00:05:23.530 --> 00:05:24.360
like everybody else?

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:34.000
Frankly, this unending quest for fresh human
flesh gets to be rather one-note.

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:38.860
And what's worse, these unstoppable killing
machines are often willing to devour the nearest

00:05:38.860 --> 00:05:42.540
member of their family in the name of a good
old-fashioned blood meal.

00:05:42.980 --> 00:05:51.240
“Come on, mom… come on, mom… ahhhhh!"

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:52.620
Enough is enough.

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:57.160
Can we please get some concrete answers as
to what makes these unspeakable monstrosities

00:05:57.160 --> 00:05:57.660
tick?

00:05:58.540 --> 00:05:59.680
"Brains!"

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:03.780
"Help!

00:06:04.040 --> 00:06:04.660
Help!"

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:12.200
Apparently when humans die and become zombies,
their first instinct is to gather in herds.

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:16.420
At least, that's the takeaway from pretty
much every show about these grim, ungodly

00:06:16.420 --> 00:06:16.920
ghouls.

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:21.860
Sure, there's still the occasional solo zombie
straggler that pops up from time to time,

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:24.000
but that's usually just for the sake of a
jump scare.

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:29.200
The really serious threat arrives when a gigantic
group of zombie deadbeats stumbles onto the

00:06:29.260 --> 00:06:29.760
scene.

00:06:37.940 --> 00:06:41.590
Whether we're talking about an intimate group
of like-minded zombies gathering in a safe

00:06:41.590 --> 00:06:46.860
environment, or a mega-herd of zombies come
to eat everyone's brains this very instant,

00:06:46.860 --> 00:06:51.040
the burning question remains the same: Why
is this supposed to be the natural behavior

00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:52.300
of zombies in the first place?

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:54.640
They're not getting more food this way.

00:06:54.740 --> 00:06:55.260
Just look at them.

00:06:55.420 --> 00:06:58.580
They're going to be hungry all the time if
they insist on traveling in those kinds of

00:06:58.580 --> 00:07:01.680
numbers… because zombies are greedy and
selfish.

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:03.400
"It's weird, eh?"

00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:14.520
Whether it's the creatures in I Am Legend
or those horrific monsters in Zombieland,

00:07:14.740 --> 00:07:17.080
these creatures almost always succumb to a
herd mentality.

00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:20.480
Not that anyone really ever bothers to explain
why.

00:07:20.480 --> 00:07:22.960
The closest we ever get to a concert answer
is this:

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:30.220
For a moment, let's turn our attention from
the undead to the living.

00:07:30.360 --> 00:07:35.470
At their root, zombies are a bonafide medical
curiosity that cause uncontrollable outbreaks

00:07:35.470 --> 00:07:37.880
and exhibit horrific symptoms that worsen
over time.

00:07:38.240 --> 00:07:42.190
Some shows like The Walking Dead never confront
the quarantine issue by making the zombie

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:45.460
virus some sort of blanket sickness that everyone
eventually contracts.

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:50.380
But more often than not, containing and controlling
the outbreak is the core plot point in a zombie

00:07:50.380 --> 00:07:50.880
film.

00:07:51.020 --> 00:07:52.720
Take the movie Quarantine, for example.

00:07:55.440 --> 00:07:59.450
So here's a question: if a zombie outbreak
affects continents and eventually the entire

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:02.860
globe, what happens to the people who live
on remote islands?

00:08:03.060 --> 00:08:05.920
Sure, it's easy to rule out the bigger players
like Great Britain.

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:09.800
After all, the film 28 Days Later takes place
on that particular island nation.

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:14.720
But what about smaller, more out-of-the-way
locations — like that faraway island in

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:17.440
the life-affirmingly awful film House of the
Dead?

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:22.880
Does Hawaii remain an island paradise… or
does everybody who live there also get infected

00:08:22.880 --> 00:08:24.760
in the event of a zombie virus outbreak?

00:08:25.360 --> 00:08:29.360
What about Madagascar… is this cute little
guy gonna get turned into a zombie?

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:38.520
Oftentimes, a zombie outbreak is shrouded
in secrecy at the beginning of the story.

00:08:38.820 --> 00:08:43.470
In order to ratchet up the tension, the protagonist
is often left completely in the dark regarding

00:08:43.470 --> 00:08:46.640
the increasingly undead state of the world
around him or her.

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:50.640
"No, I haven't got any change."

00:08:51.240 --> 00:08:55.820
Sometimes, it seems like the zombie apocalypse
took place while a healthy chunk of the world

00:08:55.820 --> 00:08:57.820
was getting some good old-fashioned shut-eye.

00:08:58.180 --> 00:08:59.440
“Sweetie, are you okay?"

00:09:06.960 --> 00:09:11.580
Sure, that totally works for zombie stories
that came out before social media was a thing,

00:09:11.590 --> 00:09:15.910
but films and television shows that take place
after the rise of Mark Zuckerberg needs to

00:09:15.910 --> 00:09:17.580
start taking Facebook into account.

00:09:17.900 --> 00:09:21.940
Let's get real here: What if this woman was
loitering around your neighborhood?

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:26.600
Imagine if these ghouls spontaneously erupted
from the soil of your local cemetery.

00:09:27.320 --> 00:09:30.320
Wouldn't someone try capturing these precious
moments on their smartphone?

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:34.140
Wouldn't a few folks decide to share the spooktacular
sights on Instagram?

00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:39.000
What we're trying to say here is: The idea
of a zombie apocalypse that isn't thoroughly

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:41.440
trumpeted on social media is patently absurd.

00:09:41.700 --> 00:09:43.620
Not to mention totally unrealistic.

00:09:44.780 --> 00:09:49.160
Here's another aspect of zombie anatomy that's
hard for us to wrap our heads around: They

00:09:49.160 --> 00:09:52.980
basically live off of nothing, all the time
— and seemingly forever.

00:09:53.640 --> 00:09:57.940
But even after they've just enjoyed some human
flesh, they still act like they're totally

00:09:57.940 --> 00:09:58.440
starving...

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:02.260
They even act that way after a gosh-darned,
bonafide feeding frenzy.

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:05.280
Like, all these zombies literally just ate.

00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:13.779
This zombie didn't even finish eating the
nice old lady, and now he's making moves on

00:10:13.780 --> 00:10:14.760
this other dude?

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:15.640
Such a waste!

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:19.980
What we've learned from all of this is that
zombies are basically impossible to satisfy.

00:10:20.620 --> 00:10:23.340
"Joey, I am not into dead guys!"

00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:24.340
"Huh?"

00:10:25.660 --> 00:10:28.320
Is there any rhyme or reason to this zombie
bloodlust?

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:30.700
Let's think rationally about it for a second.

00:10:31.050 --> 00:10:35.140
If eighty or ninety percent of the population
are turned into zombies, it makes sense that

00:10:35.140 --> 00:10:37.700
fresh human flesh would be a hot commodity
indeed.

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:41.740
But a few years down the line, it would be
nearly impossible for these zombies to find

00:10:41.900 --> 00:10:43.620
any food to shovel into their bellies.

00:10:44.090 --> 00:10:48.280
They evidently don't need to eat people in
order to survive — they're dead! — so

00:10:48.280 --> 00:10:51.030
why are they always so pumped to be eating
everybody anyway?

00:10:51.240 --> 00:10:54.600
And yet, there they go, skulking around in
search of another bite.

00:10:55.020 --> 00:10:59.020
But if zombies are willing to snack on the
occasional dead deer like this gentleman here,

00:10:59.020 --> 00:11:00.560
why this obsession with eating people?

00:11:01.450 --> 00:11:05.760
And after they've chomped on an unlucky human,
do zombies ever crave something ice-cold and

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:07.460
refreshing to wash it all down with?

00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:08.920
You can see the problem here.

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:10.920
These guys must be extremely dehydrated.

00:11:11.180 --> 00:11:15.240
Once again, the question of nutrition becomes
particularly sticky with long-running shows

00:11:15.240 --> 00:11:16.180
like The Walking Dead.

00:11:16.700 --> 00:11:19.700
All these years later, how are the walkers
even moving at this point?

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:22.640
We're all familiar with the sight of a bloody
zombie.

00:11:22.900 --> 00:11:25.260
In fact, no one even bats an eye at the sight
anymore.

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:29.680
But what about all those uninfected people
who accidentally get covered in zombie blood?

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:34.380
The Walking Dead literally has their heroes
cover themselves in zombie guts to sneak through

00:11:34.380 --> 00:11:36.640
the undead zombie gridlock undetected.

00:11:37.100 --> 00:11:38.360
How on Earth is that safe?

00:11:39.220 --> 00:11:43.000
We know that a zombie bite is almost always
fatal and will almost definitely turn you

00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:43.680
into a zombie.

00:11:43.920 --> 00:11:46.100
Even a zombie scratch can become a health
hazard.

00:11:47.380 --> 00:11:47.880
“Mark?"

00:11:51.640 --> 00:11:52.140
"Wait…"

00:11:55.160 --> 00:11:58.780
So how and why is it OK to be covered in fresh
zombie blood?

00:11:59.140 --> 00:12:00.900
Why don't those humans get infected?

00:12:01.380 --> 00:12:05.260
They're bound to have a little scratch on
them where the zombie blood can get in, right?

00:12:05.680 --> 00:12:09.720
In the end, it's never going to make total
sense.These are all just movies about silly

00:12:09.720 --> 00:12:10.480
made-up monsters.

